 cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $Y$ is a function $F(y)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(y)=P(Y\\le y).\n$$\n\nTo compute the probability of a random variable $Y$ over an interval, we can use the rule\n\n$$\nP(a<Y\\le b)=F(b)-F(a).\n$$\n\nHere, we want to compute $P(1<Y<\\frac{5}{2}).$ However, this interval is stated in the form $a<Y<b,$ not $a<Y\\le b.$\n\nSo first, we must convert the interval $1<Y<\\frac{5}{2}$ to the form $a<Y\\le b.$ Looking at the given possible values of $Y,$ we see that $Y<\\frac{5}{2}$ is equivalent to $Y\\le 2.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(1<Y<\\frac{5}{2}) & =P(1<Y\\le 2) \\\\  & =F(2)-F(1) \\\\  & =0.7-0.3 \\\\  & =0.4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535677 true] [17592186360750 1000 #edb/ref 17592186360751 13194139535677 true] [17592186360750 1000 #edb/ref 17592186360752 13194139535677 true] [17592186360750 1000 #edb/ref 17592186360753 13194139535677 true] [17592186360750 1000 #edb/ref 17592186360754 13194139535677 true] [17592186360750 1000 #edb/ref 17592186360755 13194139535677 true] [17592186360750 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535677 true] [17592186360750 1041 "selection" 13194139535677 true] [17592186360750 1104 #edb/ref 17592186360753 13194139535677 true] [17592186360750 1110 #uuid "4a6fafb2-5098-5a28-af87-16e659d7faec" 13194139535677 true] [17592186360751 1034 "0.6" 13194139535677 true] [17592186360751 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535677 true] [17592186360751 1111 #uuid "d041c975-2fcd-5824-98a8-6ec86e141af2" 13194139535677 true] [17592186360752 1034 "0.2" 13194139535677 true] [17592186360752 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535677 true] [17592186360752 1111 #uuid "e8abe744-ca5b-5939-bc85-330a42777518" 13194139535677 true] [17592186360753 1034 "0.4" 13194139535677 true] [17592186360753 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535677 true] [17592186360753 1111 #uuid "d7f7cf87-3f81-5498-a2a7-9a759a9ce3f7" 13194139535677 true] [17592186360754 1034 "0.3" 13194139535677 true] [17592186360754 1103 